This appears to be a CBP ruling on portable steel storage units. The candidates are heading 8609 (containers specially designed for carriage by one or more modes of transport) and heading 9406 (prefabricated buildings). Because the unit is not specially designed for carriage, is shipped flat and assembled after import, and is used as storage on site, 9406 is the likely heading. Steel prefabricated buildings fall under 9406.90 (formerly 9406.00), and the current 10-digit number is 9406.90.0030 for prefabricated buildings of iron or steel.

In the HTSUS, 9406.10 covers wooden buildings. 9406.90.00 covers other, with 9406.90.0030 for "Of iron or steel" and 9406.90.0080 for other, so the steel unit falls under 9406.90.0030. The subheading was restructured in 2022, which gave 9406.90.0030 (Of iron or steel) and 9406.90.0080 (Other).

{"hts_code": "9406.90.0030", "reason": "A flat-packed steel storage unit assembled after import and not specially designed for carriage is a prefabricated building of iron or steel under heading 9406, not a container of heading 8609."}
